SPS Linux live TTY

This disc boots a console. It does not partition disks.

1. Plug in or identify the destination disk (lsblk).
2. Partition and format it yourself, then mount it on /mnt.
3. Run:  setup --target /mnt
   Or just: setup
   and point the target screen at /mnt.

Optional: setup --plan --profile plasma-full --target /mnt

Recipes for sps-core and sps-extra are in /usr/src/sps. Package
builds run on this live system into the mounted target. A Plasma
install compiles Qt and KDE from source and takes a long time.

Kernel modules match the kernel on this disc. NVIDIA modules still
need that kernel after the first boot of the installed system.

Root has an open shell on the live image. Set passwords after install.
